  fraction of the symmetric lift surviving the shuffle: 6%, with a CI covering 0 and a per-seed
  range straddling it. P7 IS CONTRADICTED: the lift does NOT survive a degree-preserving shuffle, it dies
  like the own-vs-mate gap did (+0.056 -> +0.003). So the study-context effect is NOT generic series/batch
  variance that any TF-gene map of the right degree sequence would read out -- it runs THROUGH the real
  regulons: inside a GEO series a TF's actual targets move together, which is a stronger and more
  specific claim than the one predicted, and it is the same mechanism class the 0.344 baseline rests on.

  ROUTE (V-026's language). This is TF-perturbing (knockTF), masked throughout, and it concerns
  106 of 643 scored experiments (16%), 52 of them in the filtered 279. It does NOT move the
  0.344 baseline, which stands; it does not license calling that baseline mostly study context, and it
  says nothing about the 488 scored experiments with no study-mate at all. What it DOES license: on
  the rows where the test is possible, being in the same GEO series is worth about as much to a TF's
  score as being the TF that was perturbed, so a study-controlled baseline is the honest lower bound.
